  "worked_solution": "The left-hand side is a perfect square. Therefore, we can solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-8)^{2} & =-25 \\\\ x-8 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-25} \\\\ x-8 & =\\pm 5\\,\\text{i} \\\\ x & =8\\pm 5\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=8+5\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=8-5\\,\\text{i}.$",
